From 2a10b9f46a2e92adf746b416d3b74269de09d9fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 03:56:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Harden nginx jails, port 80 handling and secrets, and add
 feature tests

- Use fail2ban's own nginx-botsearch filter and stop counting 404s in
  nginx-bad-request (400/444 only, 10 hits in 10 minutes). The old custom
  filter is backed up and removed on re-run.
- Warn when running inside WSL or without systemd.
- Port 80 busy: let the user stop that service, continue, or skip the web
  server step, instead of dropping the step. Treat httpd as Apache.
- Keep the MySQL root login only in /root/.my.cnf (mode 600): not printed,
  not logged, not kept in CFG. An existing /root/.my.cnf is left alone.
- uninstall: never delete fail2ban's stock nginx-botsearch filter; keep
  /root/.my.cnf, and print how to undo Bun in /opt/bun and a stopped service.
- Add tests/features.sh (presets, feature dependencies, port 80 flow, jail
  regex) and let setup.sh be sourced by tests.
- Keep ShellCheck clean with the README command; document the changes.
